@* Each color where it's used: the page, a card on it (Surface), fills inside the card, each a step
   further from it, a sunken area holding a card of its own (a board's column), and an overlay with
   a border and a shadow, as menus and popovers draw over the card. *@
<Box Padding="4" Bg="Color.Background" Border="1" Radius="Radius.Lg" Grow>
    <Stack Gap="3">
        <TextBlock Size="TextSize.Sm" Color="Color.Muted">Background</TextBlock>
        <Box Padding="4" Bg="Color.Surface" Border="1" Radius="Radius.Lg">
            <Stack Gap="3">
                <TextBlock Size="TextSize.Sm" Color="Color.Muted">Surface</TextBlock>
                <Grid Columns="new() { Base = 1, Sm = 3 }" Gap="3">
                    <Box Padding="3" Bg="Color.FillSubtle" Radius="Radius.Md">FillSubtle</Box>
                    <Box Padding="3" Bg="Color.Fill" Radius="Radius.Md">Fill</Box>
                    <Box Padding="3" Bg="Color.FillStrong" Radius="Radius.Md">FillStrong</Box>
                </Grid>
                <Box Padding="3" Bg="Color.SurfaceSunken" Radius="Radius.Md">
                    <Stack Gap="2">
                        <TextBlock Size="TextSize.Sm" Color="Color.Muted">SurfaceSunken</TextBlock>
                        <Box Padding="3" Bg="Color.Surface" Border="1" Radius="Radius.Md">A card in it</Box>
                    </Stack>
                </Box>
                <Box Padding="3" Bg="Color.SurfaceOverlay" Border="1" Shadow="Shadow.Lg" Radius="Radius.Lg" MaxWidth="Length.Rem(16)">
                    SurfaceOverlay
                    <TextBlock Size="TextSize.Sm" Color="Color.Muted">A menu or popover</TextBlock>
                </Box>
            </Stack>
        </Box>
    </Stack>
</Box>
